I am on my bed.
There is wifi in the room.
My mobile is in my hand.
I call my parents in Mexico.
My parents are on the call.
There is worry in my mother's voice.
She asks, "Maya, are you okay?"
I say, "Yes Mom, I am absolutely fine."
My father asks, "Maya, where are you?"
"Are you in your room?"
I say, "Yes Papa, I am in my new room."
Mom asks, "Is everything fine there?"
I say, "Yes, everything is fine here."
Papa asks, "Are you happy?"
I smile.
I say, "Yes, I am happy."
"But I am a little tired."
Mom says, "Okay, good night Maya."
I say, "Good night, Mom."
"Good night, Papa."
Now my room is quiet again.
